{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1856","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1856","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1856\",\"parent_revision\":\"527860b5980f38c3ee1ccb630a415bc5b8f4c32e59e012b75fef4964a5d48ea1\",\"root_revision\":\"527860b5980f38c3ee1ccb630a415bc5b8f4c32e59e012b75fef4964a5d48ea1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Surface stall_detected on in-progress tasks via last-activity timestamp\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Expose stall detection signal from the existing last_activity timestamp so the implement-feature orchestrator uses an authoritative data source instead of transcript parsing.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. task_status_hook.py last-activity write location | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py \u2014 writes last-activity on every PostToolUse\\n2. Task model last_activity field | AVAILABLE | sam_schema/core/models.py line 150 \u2014 last_activity: datetime | None\\n3. sam_plan action='status' and action='ready' output schema | AVAILABLE | SAM MCP server; current output does not include stall_minutes or stall_detected\\n4. implement-feature SKILL Agent Health Check section | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 100-128 (approximate)\\n5. SAM_STALL_THRESHOLD_MIN configurable env var | DERIVABLE | design decision; default 10 minutes is conventional but needs confirmation\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 no new data required; pure signal amplification of existing fields.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `sam_plan(action='status')` response includes `stall_minutes: int | null` and `stall_detected: bool` for each `in-progress` task, computed as `now - last_activity`\\n- [ ] `stall_detected` flips to `true` when `stall_minutes` exceeds `SAM_STALL_THRESHOLD_MIN` (default 10, configurable via env var)\\n- [ ] implement-feature SKILL.md Agent Health Check reads `stall_detected` from `sam_plan(action='status')` as the primary stall signal; falls through to transcript parsing only when `last_activity` is null\\n- [ ] New unit test: task with `last_activity` 11 minutes in the past + `SAM_STALL_THRESHOLD_MIN=10` \u2192 `stall_detected: true`; task with `last_activity` 5 minutes in the past \u2192 `stall_detected: false`\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` \u2014 zero errors on modified files\\n- [ ] `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` \u2014 zero errors on modified files\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model (last_activity at line 150)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 status/ready queries (add stall_minutes + stall_detected computation)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Agent Health Check section (update to use stall_detected)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 reference for last-activity write logic (read-only for this item)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 new or extended test for stall detection\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **implement-feature orchestrator performing an agent health check**, I want **stall detection based on the `last_activity` timestamp already written by `task_status_hook.py`** so that **I don't re-spawn an agent based on subjective silence observation when an authoritative per-task timestamp is already on disk**.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='status')` output for an `in-progress` task includes `stall_minutes` and `stall_detected`.\\n- With `SAM_STALL_THRESHOLD_MIN=5` and a task whose `last-activity` is 7 minutes old, `stall_detected: true` appears.\\n- New unit test in `tests_sam/` sets a fake `last_activity` 10 minutes in the past and asserts `stall_detected: true`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **surface stall_detected on in-progress tasks via last-activity timestamp** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: State management + dashboard progress tracking (features 5, 6)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`task_status_hook.py` writes `last-activity` on every PostToolUse (Write/Edit/Bash), and the `Task` model persists it as `last_activity: datetime | None` (models.py line 150). No code reads this field to detect or act on stalled agents. The implement-feature SKILL (lines 100\u2013128) defines an \\\"Agent Health Check\\\" but the only signal is \\\"~10 minutes of silence\\\" observed subjectively by the orchestrator via JSONL transcript analysis \u2014 the timestamp already on disk in the task file is never consulted.\\n\\nSymptom: the orchestrator re-spawns based on transcript parsing instead of the authoritative per-task timestamp the hook has been writing all along. Stalled tasks are detected late or not at all.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`sam_plan(action='ready')` and `sam_plan(action='status')` return, for each `in-progress` task, computed fields `stall_minutes: int | null` and `stall_detected: bool`. A plan-level or env-configurable threshold (`SAM_STALL_THRESHOLD_MIN`, default 10) controls when `stall_detected` flips to true. The implement-feature SKILL Agent Health Check reads `stall_detected` first and falls through to transcript analysis only when `last_activity` is missing.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"048f617df6049e6bf01dbb799bb7df76bd11c5434f85cd8c87ef118da3372f47\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-i_A\"}"}